{"route":"/docs/5.3/getting-started/download/","version":"5.3","renderedVersion":"5.3","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Download","level":1},"lead":{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Download Bootstrap to get the compiled CSS and JavaScript, source code, or include it with your favorite package managers like npm, RubyGems, and more."},"blocks":[{"id":"compiled-css-and-js","type":"heading","en":"Compiled CSS and JS","level":2},{"id":"compiled-css-and-js--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Download ready-to-use compiled code for <strong>Bootstrap v5.3.9</strong> to easily drop into your project, which includes:"},{"id":"compiled-css-and-js--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"compiled-css-and-js--item-1","type":"item","en":"Compiled and minified CSS bundles (see <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contents#css-files\">CSS files comparison</a>)"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"compiled-css-and-js--item-2","type":"item","en":"Compiled and minified JavaScript plugins (see <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contents#js-files\">JS files comparison</a>)"}]}]},{"id":"compiled-css-and-js--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"This doesn’t include documentation, source files, or any optional JavaScript dependencies like Popper."},{"id":"compiled-css-and-js--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/releases/download/v5.3.9/bootstrap-5.3.9-dist.zip\">Download</a>"},{"id":"source-files","type":"heading","en":"Source files","level":2},{"id":"source-files--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Compile Bootstrap with your own asset pipeline by downloading our source Sass, JavaScript, and documentation files. This option requires some additional tooling:"},{"id":"source-files--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"source-files--item-1","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contribute#sass\">Sass compiler</a> for compiling Sass source files into CSS files"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"source-files--item-2","type":"item","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer\">Autoprefixer</a> for CSS vendor prefixing"}]}]},{"id":"source-files--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Should you require our full set of <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contribute#tooling-setup\">build tools</a>, they are included for developing Bootstrap and its docs, but they’re likely unsuitable for your own purposes."},{"id":"source-files--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/archive/v5.3.9.zip\">Download source</a>"},{"id":"examples","type":"heading","en":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"examples--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"If you want to download and examine our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/examples\">examples</a>, you can grab the already built examples:"},{"id":"examples--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/releases/download/v5.3.9/bootstrap-5.3.9-examples.zip\">Download Examples</a>"},{"id":"cdn-via-jsdelivr","type":"heading","en":"CDN via jsDelivr","level":2},{"id":"cdn-via-jsdelivr--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Skip the download with <a href=\"https://www.jsdelivr.com/\">jsDelivr</a> to deliver cached version of Bootstrap’s compiled CSS and JS to your project."},{"id":"cdn-via-jsdelivr--code-1","type":"code","value":"<link href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.9/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" integrity=\"sha384-yEPZ7jP9S0QKiUQ0m3jjsO4ProIW7wvR9gXkI7JOGa2XVsw53Yke2bsdkBbjmmiX\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.9/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-WyOxWvTyr1QaMPfiPJSv76iReVthorl5uWlFtZPyK0IEB0hGzo9y5Bp9mYanr8Bu\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>","language":"html"},{"id":"cdn-via-jsdelivr--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"If you’re using our compiled JavaScript and prefer to include Popper separately, add Popper before our JS, via a CDN preferably."},{"id":"cdn-via-jsdelivr--code-2","type":"code","value":"<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@popperjs/core@2.11.8/dist/umd/popper.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-I7E8VVD/ismYTF4hNIPjVp/Zjvgyol6VFvRkX/vR+Vc4jQkC+hVqc2pM8ODewa9r\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.9/dist/js/bootstrap.min.js\" integrity=\"sha384-89aa4glufciPv46aKltztWQEmk+Tu9W2RhzXr6VcnUUEub7F8+06RcL2RYLCOHUq\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>","language":"html"},{"id":"alternative-cdns","type":"heading","en":"Alternative CDNs","level":3},{"id":"alternative-cdns--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"We recommend <a href=\"https://www.jsdelivr.com/\">jsDelivr</a> and use it ourselves in our documentation. However, in some cases—like in some specific countries or environments—you may need to use other CDN providers like <a href=\"https://cdnjs.com/\">cdnjs</a> or <a href=\"https://unpkg.com/\">unpkg</a>."},{"id":"alternative-cdns--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"You’ll find the same files on these CDN providers, albeit with different URLs. With cdnjs, you can <a href=\"https://cdnjs.com/libraries/bootstrap\">use this direct Bootstrap package link</a> to copy and paste ready-to-use HTML snippets for each dist file from any version of Bootstrap."},{"id":"alternative-cdns--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"alternative-cdns--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>If the SRI hashes differ for a given file, you shouldn’t use the files from that CDN, because it means that the file was modified by someone else.</strong>"}]},{"id":"alternative-cdns--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Note that you should compare same length hashes, e.g. <code>sha384</code> with <code>sha384</code>, otherwise it’s expected for them to be different.\nAs such, you can use an online tool like <a href=\"https://srihash.org/\">SRI Hash Generator</a> to make sure that the hashes are the same for a given file.\nAlternatively, assuming you have OpenSSL installed, you can achieve the same from the CLI, for example:"},{"id":"alternative-cdns--code-1","type":"code","value":"openssl dgst -sha384 -binary bootstrap.min.js | openssl base64 -A","language":"sh"},{"id":"package-managers","type":"heading","en":"Package managers","level":2},{"id":"package-managers--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Pull in Bootstrap’s <strong>source files</strong> into nearly any project with some of the most popular package managers. No matter the package manager, Bootstrap will <strong>require a <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contribute#sass\">Sass compiler</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/postcss/autoprefixer\">Autoprefixer</a></strong> for a setup that matches our official compiled versions."},{"id":"npm","type":"heading","en":"npm","level":3},{"id":"npm--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Install Bootstrap in your Node.js powered apps with <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/bootstrap\">the npm package</a>:"},{"id":"npm--code-1","type":"code","value":"npm install bootstrap@5.3.9","language":"sh"},{"id":"npm--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"<code>const bootstrap = require(&#39;bootstrap&#39;)</code> or <code>import bootstrap from &#39;bootstrap&#39;</code> will load all of Bootstrap’s plugins onto a <code>bootstrap</code> object.\nThe <code>bootstrap</code> module itself exports all of our plugins. You can manually load Bootstrap’s plugins individually by loading the <code>/js/dist/*.js</code> files under the package’s top-level directory."},{"id":"npm--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap’s <code>package.json</code> contains some additional metadata under the following keys:"},{"id":"npm--list-1","type":"list","tag":"ul","items":[{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"npm--item-1","type":"item","en":"<code>sass</code> - path to Bootstrap’s main <a href=\"https://sass-lang.com/\">Sass</a> source file"}]},{"tag":"li","body":[{"id":"npm--item-2","type":"item","en":"<code>style</code> - path to Bootstrap’s non-minified CSS that’s been compiled using the default settings (no customization)"}]}]},{"id":"npm--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"npm--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Get started with Bootstrap via npm with our starter project!</strong> Head to the <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/examples/tree/main/sass-js\">Sass &amp; JS example</a> template repository to see how to build and customize Bootstrap in your own npm project. Includes Sass compiler, Autoprefixer, Stylelint, PurgeCSS, and Bootstrap Icons."}]},{"id":"yarn","type":"heading","en":"yarn","level":3},{"id":"yarn--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Install Bootstrap in your Node.js powered apps with <a href=\"https://yarnpkg.com/en/package/bootstrap\">the yarn package</a>:"},{"id":"yarn--code-1","type":"code","value":"yarn add bootstrap@5.3.9","language":"sh"},{"id":"yarn--note-1","type":"note","tone":"warning","body":[{"id":"yarn--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"<strong>Yarn 2+ (aka Yarn Berry) doesn’t support the <code>node_modules</code> directory by default</strong>: using our <a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/examples/tree/main/sass-js\">Sass &amp; JS example</a> needs some adjustments:"},{"id":"yarn--code-2","type":"code","value":"yarn config set nodeLinker node-modules # Use the node_modules linker\ntouch yarn.lock # Create an empty yarn.lock file\nyarn install # Install the dependencies\nyarn start # Start the project","language":"sh"}]},{"id":"bun","type":"heading","en":"Bun","level":3},{"id":"bun--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Install Bootstrap in your Bun or Node.js powered apps with <a href=\"https://bun.sh/\">the Bun CLI</a>:"},{"id":"bun--code-1","type":"code","value":"bun add bootstrap@5.3.9","language":"sh"},{"id":"rubygems","type":"heading","en":"RubyGems","level":3},{"id":"rubygems--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Install Bootstrap in your Ruby apps using <a href=\"https://bundler.io/\">Bundler</a> (<strong>recommended</strong>) and <a href=\"https://rubygems.org/\">RubyGems</a> by adding the following line to your <a href=\"https://bundler.io/guides/gemfile.html\"><code>Gemfile</code></a>:"},{"id":"rubygems--code-1","type":"code","value":"gem 'bootstrap', '~> 5.3.9'","language":"ruby"},{"id":"rubygems--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Alternatively, if you’re not using Bundler, you can install the gem by running this command:"},{"id":"rubygems--code-2","type":"code","value":"gem install bootstrap -v 5.3.9","language":"sh"},{"id":"rubygems--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap-rubygem/blob/main/README.md\">See the gem’s README</a> for further details."},{"id":"composer","type":"heading","en":"Composer","level":3},{"id":"composer--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"You can also install and manage Bootstrap’s Sass and JavaScript using <a href=\"https://getcomposer.org/\">Composer</a>:"},{"id":"composer--code-1","type":"code","value":"composer require twbs/bootstrap:5.3.9","language":"sh"},{"id":"nuget","type":"heading","en":"NuGet","level":3},{"id":"nuget--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"If you develop in .NET Framework, you can also install and manage Bootstrap’s <a href=\"https://www.nuget.org/packages/bootstrap/\">CSS</a> or <a href=\"https://www.nuget.org/packages/bootstrap.sass/\">Sass</a> and JavaScript using <a href=\"https://www.nuget.org/\">NuGet</a>. Newer projects should use <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/client-side/libman/\">libman</a> or another method as NuGet is designed for compiled code, not frontend assets."},{"id":"nuget--code-1","type":"code","value":"Install-Package bootstrap","language":"powershell"},{"id":"nuget--code-2","type":"code","value":"Install-Package bootstrap.sass","language":"powershell"},{"id":"intellisense-extension","type":"heading","en":"IntelliSense extension","level":2},{"id":"intellisense-extension--media-1","type":"media","html":"<img src=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/assets/img/bootstrap-intellisense-autocomplete.png\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">"},{"id":"intellisense-extension--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Install the community-maintained <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=hossaini.bootstrap-intellisense\">IntelliSense extension</a> for Visual Studio Code to get IntelliSense auto-completion for Bootstrap classes."},{"id":"intellisense-extension--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=hossaini.bootstrap-intellisense\">View in VS Code Marketplace</a>"}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/introduction"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/download"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contents"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/browsers-devices"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/javascript"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/webpack"},{"en":"Parcel","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/parcel"},{"en":"Vite","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/vite"},{"en":"Accessibility","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/accessibility"},{"en":"RFS","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/rfs"},{"en":"RTL","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/rtl"},{"en":"Contribute","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/getting-started/contribute"},{"en":"Overview","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/customize/overview"},{"en":"Sass","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/5.3/customi